<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sierra Nevada de Santa Marta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sierra <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a> de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-marta">Santa Marta</a> is an isolated mountain range on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast of northern Colombia, rising to over 5,700 metres, among the highest coastal ranges in the world. It was the home of the Tairona chiefdoms, who built stone-terraced towns such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciudad-perdida">Ciudad Perdida</a>. Their descendants, the Kogi, Arhuaco and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiwa-people">Wiwa peoples</a>, still live there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sierra-nevada-de-santa-marta.jpg" alt="Sierra Nevada de Santa Marta" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lobocordero5 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amanecer_en_la_Sierra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
